      "proposition": {
        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>Christine Edzard’s The Man With the Plan tours the country with a timely message about tackling want, disease, squalor, idleness and ignorance</p><p>A new film that addresses issues fundamental to the new prime minister’s declared mission will star Simon Callow as a historical British political figure.</p><p>The hero of The Man With the Plan is <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2012/dec/07/william-beveridge-hated-term-welfare-state\">William Beveridge</a>, who helped to lay the foundations of the postwar welfare state. It shows that the Liberal peer was much more radical than is usually assumed – and certainly far more so than Churchill anticipated when he asked Beveridge to draw up a report into the future of Britain’s fragmented social insurance and national health system after the second world war.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/film/2026/sep/01/beveridge-revisited-simon-callow-film-celebrates-the-radical-co-founder-of-britains-welfare-state\">Continue reading...</a>"
